WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.267
-Welcome back to the program.
-I like the vibe. Nice.

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:04.868
-Yeah. Well, you know,
we're talking about whiskey.

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:06.133
We want to talk about
all this stuff

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:08.000
and all the spirits
and everything you're into.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.400
But I want to talk
about the book.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.467
Congrats on this, by the way.
-Thank you.

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:14.901
-And I also want --
-Is that me on the front?

00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:16.234
-Yeah.
-Yeah, yeah, it is. Good, good.

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:17.267
Just checking you got
the right one, yeah.

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:18.601
-Yeah, yeah, it could be me.

00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:20.000
I mean, yeah,
we look like twins.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.734
I mean, but...
-We do.

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:23.067
-Did I read this right?

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:25.601
Did you want to be a magician
when you were growing up?

00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:27.968
-I probably wanted to be
a lot of things growing up,

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:30.701
yeah, but I think I did give it
a go for a little while,

00:00:30.701 --> 00:00:32.634
but I realized
I don't really have the --

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:34.133
I didn't want to put
in the work, you know?

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:37.267
I wanted to put on the outfit,
you know, the sort of the hat

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:39.100
and the cape and the wand
and all that stuff,

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.267
but actually
learning the tricks,

00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:43.033
I was just rubbish at it.

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:44.367
-So you'd just show up
and go "Aha"

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:47.100
and then "Watch me disappear"
and then leave, yeah.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.601
That was your only trick.

00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:51.634
-I could juggle a little bit,
but, I mean, come on, that's --

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:52.901
-That's something.
-That's right.

00:00:52.901 --> 00:00:54.467
I mean, I think that's why
I became an actor, right?

00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:55.767
So then I can
put on the clothes,

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:58.133
pretend to be someone,
and then not do any of the work.

00:00:58.133 --> 00:01:01.167
-Yeah. What was the --
When you were an actor,

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:02.367
obviously,
when you first started out,

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:03.868
you have to take
other jobs to support.

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:05.067
Do you remember
any of those jobs?

00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:06.901
-Oh, boy. Where to start?

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:10.267
I delivered sandwiches
by bicycle.

00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:12.400
I worked in Harrods.
I sold women's clothing.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:13.400
-Oh, in Harrods.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.234
-I sold -- Yeah, I know.
Posh, right?

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:16.767
-Yes.
-Yeah, very nice.

00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:20.300
I sold perfume and I was
a barman, as well, actually.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:23.133
In Scotland,
I worked in an Irish bar.

00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:25.434
-Wait. An Irish bar in Scotland?
-An Irish bar in Scotland.

00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:28.834
I wore a flatcap
and a very dodgy accent.

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:30.868
So, again, yeah -- and I was --
-You pretended to be Irish?

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:33.968
-[ Irish accent ]
Ah, to be sure.

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:37.200
[ Normal voice ] And I poured a
terrible pint of Guinness, so...

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.901
-That was your giveaway?
-Yeah, they had me. They had me.

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:43.667
-Yeah. The other week,
I saw you posted a photo of you

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:46.400
just walking around
wearing a kilt in New York City.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.534
-Right. That's not my dog.
-No, it's not your dog.

00:01:49.934 --> 00:01:51.300
It's a cute dog, though.
-It is a cute dog.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:52.667
-Yeah. Do people look
at you differently

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:54.067
when you're wearing a kilt?

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:55.667
-Honestly, in New York,
I think they've seen it all.

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:58.300
They don't care, do they?
-We really don't care.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:01:59.767
-I'm going to have to up
my outfit next time.

00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:01.701
I'll wear the wizard one.
That's what I'll do.

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:03.067
-Oh, you will?
-Yeah.

00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:04.067
-Well, that'll be fun next time
you come on the show.

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:05.167
-Yeah.

00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:06.734
-But I saw you're
sticking with the kilts.

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:09.100
Here's you in a kilt
on a glacier.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:12.767
-That's me in New Zealand,
on a glacier, in commando.

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:16.100
I claim to be the first person
in commando on a glacier.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.100
Thank you very much.
-Wow.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.667
That's your
little piece of history?

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:19.834
-That's it.
-Yeah.

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:21.167
-I went all the way
just to do that, yeah.

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:23.200
-Well, it goes along
to talk about this

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.834
in the new book here,
"Clanlands in New Zealand."

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:27.167
-Yeah.

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:29.501
-It's a companion piece
to the show "Men in Kilts."

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:30.634
-That's right.

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:33.100
-You travel to different
countries and you --

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.601
In this one,
you explore New Zealand.

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:37.000
-We went to New Zealand,
which is this amazing place.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.834
It's honestly -- It's a bit
like, you know, Neverland,

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:40.934
Peter Pan's Neverland.

00:02:40.934 --> 00:02:43.701
There's these islands.
There's alpine.

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:46.367
There's glaciers.
There's fjords. There's jungle.

00:02:46.367 --> 00:02:49.200
There's incredible
animal wildlife there.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.667
They've got flightless birds,
great white sharks,

00:02:51.667 --> 00:02:52.734
and, of course, you know,

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:55.000
glaciers that I wear
no underwear on.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.234
-Yeah, so smart, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:57.234 --> 00:02:59.534
-We -- Last time you were
on the show, actually,

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:02.868
we were talking about you have
your own whiskey and tequila.

00:03:02.868 --> 00:03:04.634
-I do.
-And they both won awards.

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:06.367
-Thank you.
-Congratulations.

00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:08.367
-Thank you.
The Jimmy Award, yeah.

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:09.534
-Yeah, I gave you the Jimmy --

00:03:09.534 --> 00:03:11.501
You won some
massive, major awards.

00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:14.000
And then I had a suggestion
for you last time.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.901
I don't know if you remember
this or not, but the --

00:03:15.901 --> 00:03:18.400
-Oh, vaguely, vaguely.
-I'll show a clip.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:19.434
Can we show a clip of
his last --

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:20.601
-What did you say?

00:03:20.601 --> 00:03:21.801
-You go, "Yeah, I'm going
to make a whiskey."

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.100
You don't mess around.
-Right.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.601
-You ended up winning
all these awards for it.

00:03:24.601 --> 00:03:25.934
And then you made
this amazing tequila.

00:03:25.934 --> 00:03:27.100
What is it called?

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:29.534
-It's called the
Sassenach Select El Tequileño,

00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:31.534
and we just won a couple of
gold medals for it, as well.

00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:33.067
-I mean, dude --
-What's next, right?

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:34.534
-I'm so happy.
-What do you want?

00:03:34.534 --> 00:03:35.901
We'll make it.
-Yeah.

00:03:35.901 --> 00:03:37.667
I like gin,
if you want to work on a gin.

00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:38.834
-Oh, we could do that, yeah.

00:03:38.834 --> 00:03:40.667
Jimmy's Gin?
-Ginny Fallon.

00:03:40.667 --> 00:03:42.801
Yeah, go for it. You take it.
-Ginny Fallon.

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:45.167
-You made --
-We made a gin!

00:03:45.167 --> 00:03:47.234
-Yeah, you made a gin.
-Yeah!

00:03:47.234 --> 00:03:50.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yes.

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:54.767
-And please don't tell me --
did this win an award?

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.267
-It's won several gold medals.
-Oh, my God.

00:03:56.267 --> 00:03:58.133
-I'm sorry.
-Did it really?

00:03:58.133 --> 00:04:00.400
-It really did.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:05.634
But, obviously,
I wanted to call it Jimmy's Gin,

00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:07.200
but I thought
something easier to say,

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.133
like Sassenach, right?

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:11.167
-Much easier, yes.
Sassenach, yeah.

00:04:11.167 --> 00:04:13.234
-I'm really proud of it.
It's our Wild Scottish Gin.

00:04:13.234 --> 00:04:15.567
And, honestly, I'm running
out of things to make,

00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:17.067
so next time you invite me on,
I'm gonna have to do --

00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:18.634
I don't know -- Like,
what am I going to do next?

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:21.100
-Well, actually, I have
some ingredients here

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:22.234
if you want to make...

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:24.300
-Oh, a cocktail.
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:25.934 --> 00:04:28.567
-Now we're talking. Right.

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:30.701
-Why are there --
What do we have here?

00:04:30.701 --> 00:04:33.501
Why do we have eggs?
-Eggs are good for protein.

00:04:33.501 --> 00:04:34.701
-Well, I understand.

00:04:34.701 --> 00:04:36.801
-So, we're going to make you
a Ginny Fallon.

00:04:36.801 --> 00:04:37.934
-You are?

00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:39.634
-We're going to make you
a Ginny Fallon cocktail.

00:04:39.634 --> 00:04:40.801
You're going to help me,
my friend.

00:04:40.801 --> 00:04:41.801
-I love this.

00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:42.934
-We've got in here --

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:45.501
I've been told, reliably,
that there is --

00:04:45.501 --> 00:04:46.534
[ Sniffs ]
Whoo!

00:04:46.534 --> 00:04:49.200
Yep, that is alcohol.
-Okay, yeah.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.968
-Gin. Wild Scottish Gin.
♪♪

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:54.033
We've got some lemon juice.
We've got some simple syrup.

00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:55.133
-Okay.

00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:56.234
-We're going to put
some ice in there.

00:04:56.234 --> 00:04:57.467
You're going to put
some ice in there.

00:04:57.467 --> 00:04:59.033
-Okay, here we go.
-We're gonna make this together.

00:04:59.033 --> 00:05:00.801
We're going to give
this a little shake.

00:05:00.801 --> 00:05:02.801
-Okay.

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:04.601
-I've already
messed this up, Jimmy.

00:05:04.601 --> 00:05:05.734
-You did?
-Yeah.

00:05:05.734 --> 00:05:07.400
-Were you not supposed to put --
-It's okay.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.534
-Alright, good.
-It's all going to be fine.

00:05:09.534 --> 00:05:10.868
-Why are there eggs here?

00:05:10.868 --> 00:05:12.834
-Okay, we got to put
an egg in there now.

00:05:12.834 --> 00:05:14.968
-Okay.
-I should have dry-shaken that.

00:05:14.968 --> 00:05:16.133
-That's right.
Oh, you dry-shake it.

00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:17.133
-Yeah, ever mind.

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:18.133
-Oh, you shake it
without the ice.

00:05:18.133 --> 00:05:19.567
-Yeah, right.
-Alright.

00:05:19.567 --> 00:05:22.067
Now you can't even open it.
-I can't even open it, Jimmy.

00:05:22.067 --> 00:05:25.267
-Wait.
What if we just drink from here?

00:05:25.267 --> 00:05:27.534
-Do we need the eggs?
-We don't need the eggs.

00:05:27.534 --> 00:05:30.167
-Why don't we just crack an egg.
-Yeah, crack an egg.

00:05:30.167 --> 00:05:32.667
-And put it in.
-There you go. An egg in there.

00:05:32.667 --> 00:05:34.467
-Now top that in.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:40.234
-This is fantastic.
Hey, cheers, buddy.

00:05:40.234 --> 00:05:42.567
-The Jimmy Fallon.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:42.567 --> 00:05:44.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:48.133 --> 00:05:50.133
Not bad. It's actually --
The gin makes it taste good.

00:05:50.133 --> 00:05:52.000
Yeah. Sam Heughan, everybody.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.534
Congrats on the gin,

00:05:53.534 --> 00:05:57.634
and, of course, the new book,
"Clanlands in New Zealand:

00:05:57.634 --> 00:05:59.734
Kiwis, Kilts,
and an Adventure Down Under,"

00:05:59.734 --> 00:06:01.234
is available November 7th.

00:06:01.234 --> 00:06:02.634
Stick around.

00:06:02.634 --> 00:06:04.133
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show," everybody.

